items.acceptance:
- Acceptance:
  - an ISM-only NEWS fixture runs through `run_v1_simple_gemini_newsroom` to a post whose one card shows the title and date and no survey figure;
  - T2, T3 and T4 pass on the live head, and the post-visual and native-editorial test files pass;
  - the fix is integrated into the ContentOps operating root with a live tag and a rollback tag, as babd311d was.
  Never run the full suite in the live root: it rewrites 56 tracked files.

- Acceptance:
  - before and after renders, side by side, for the Southwest filing, a CPI or PPI release, a digest and a CC-267 title card, at 1080x1350 and the X size;
  - focused tests, including a single left edge across blocks and a figure chosen over a date;
  - integrated into the ContentOps root with a live tag and a rollback tag; the next published piece carries the new card.

- Acceptance:
  - tests: the reader order; a missing key fails by name; nothing printed;
  - integrated in the ContentOps root with live and rollback tags;
  - with Jim's Threads values in Credential Manager and the two names gone from the environment, the Threads probe reads READY_NON_BROWSER_BINDING (its API-surface ready state);
  - after Jim's move-script run, the user environment holds none of the ContentOps names, and the next piece posts on every destination.

- Acceptance:
  - registry tests: a general public event can take each mode, a breaking event still prefers the brief, and a mode without its evidence is refused;
  - integrated with live and rollback tags;
  - one real piece in either mode goes out within a week.

- Acceptance:
  - tests: each route's payload has no borrowed-host link, and the guard refuses one planted in each destination's text;
  - integrated with a live tag and a rollback tag;
  - Ops Product re-enables CapitalChronicle-PlanStatusPosts-V1, and the next status post reads back with no site link;
  - the profile check is reported.

- Acceptance:
  - tests: one result post per ended plan, exactly-once; the count is right; no claim wording passes;
  - the first plan that ends after integration gives one result post per working destination, read back;
  - integrated with a live tag and a rollback tag.

- Acceptance:
  - tests: each public builder renders ET, and a guard test refuses a final payload containing "GMT+7" or "UTC+7";
  - the next article read back shows ET only;
  - integrated with a live tag and a rollback tag.

- Acceptance:
  - tests: a reused, near-duplicate or missing lead image is refused; the scenarios section is required in the article and in each social copy; the daily cap holds;
  - the next two published pieces each carry an image never used before and a scenarios section, read back on Substack and the social destinations;
  - integrated with a live tag and a rollback tag.

- Acceptance:
  - tests: a row with `scenario_analysis` composes the why block on each destination within its length limit; no target, R:R, size, fill or P&L reaches the copy; a row without `scenario_analysis` still posts;
  - the next new-plan post carries the why block on every destination, read back;
  - integrated with live and rollback tags.

- Acceptance:
  - copy proof: a touched producer file triggers one refresh within 60 s; a second touch inside the gap waits; an unchanged store is not copied again; the 20-minute backstop still runs;
  - on CPI day (Tue 10 Nov, release 13:30Z) the desk's CPI page shows the admitted print within 60 s of its admission readback, and the arrival result within 60 s of its RESULT.md.
